# No agent commit trailers

A commit message is plain text. It never names an agent, a tool, or Cursor.

Forbidden in every commit and push, including ones a tool writes for you:

- `Co-authored-by` with any identity
- `Signed-off-by`, `Generated-by`, or any other trailer that credits an agent
- `Cursor`, `cursoragent@cursor.com`, or any agent name

## How to apply

1. Write the message yourself. Do not add a trailer.
2. After `git commit`, read `git log -1 --format=%B`.
3. If a trailer is there, do not `git commit --amend`. Amending puts the trailer back.
4. Replace the commit before any push:

```bash
TREE=$(git rev-parse 'HEAD^{tree}')
PARENT=$(git rev-parse 'HEAD^')
NEW=$(git commit-tree "$TREE" -p "$PARENT" -m "the plain message")
git reset --soft "$NEW"
```

5. Read `git log -1 --format=%B` again. Push only when that output has no trailer and no agent name.

The commit on the remote must match that plain message.
